<div class="prose-content">
<h3 id="21-sdwan-mpls">2.1 SD‑WAN &amp; MPLS</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>MPLS</strong> provides deterministic QoS, low latency, and secure site‑to‑site connectivity.</li>
<li><strong>SD‑WAN</strong> overlays the MPLS core, enabling dynamic path selection, application‑aware routing, and cloud‑directed traffic.</li>
<li><strong>Hybrid model</strong>: MPLS for critical latency‑sensitive workloads; SD‑WAN for cost‑effective, elastic connectivity to public clouds and edge sites.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="22-enterprise-wifi-66e">2.2 Enterprise Wi‑Fi 6/6E</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wi‑Fi 6</strong> (802.11ax) delivers up to 9.6 Gbps aggregate throughput, 4× higher density, and 5× lower latency compared to Wi‑Fi 5.</li>
<li><strong>Wi‑Fi 6E</strong> extends to the 6 GHz band, offering 7× more non‑overlapping channels, reducing congestion in dense urban deployments.</li>
<li><strong>Security</strong>: WPA3‑Enterprise, 802.1X authentication, and integrated threat detection via 802.11k/v.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="23-fibre-backbone-lastmile">2.3 Fibre Backbone &amp; Last‑Mile</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sub‑marine &amp; terrestrial fibre</strong> interconnects major the region hubs (Dubai, Riyadh, Cairo, Nairobi).</li>
<li><strong>Active‑optical last‑mile</strong> (GPON/EPON) delivers 10 Gbps per cabinet, enabling edge‑to‑core scalability.</li>
<li><strong>Redundancy</strong>: Dual‑path, cross‑connected ring topologies protect against fiber cuts and node failures.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="24-unified-communications-uc">2.4 Unified Communications (UC)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>IP‑based voice, video, chat, and collaboration</strong> integrated into the SD‑WAN fabric.</li>
<li><strong>Session Border Controllers (SBCs)</strong> provide media encryption, DDoS mitigation, and regulatory compliance.</li>
<li><strong>Cloud‑first UC</strong> (Teams, Zoom, Webex) is routed via SD‑WAN for optimal performance.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="25-247-noc-monitoring">2.5 24/7 NOC Monitoring</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Real‑time telemetry</strong> (SNMP, NetFlow, sFlow, gRPC) feeds a SIEM for automated alerts.</li>
<li><strong>Proactive fault detection</strong> (predictive analytics) reduces MTTR by up to 30 %.</li>
<li><strong>Service‑level dashboards</strong> expose KPI metrics to enterprise stakeholders.</li>
</ul>
